        {
            "id": "5c80a03c-0831-4033-a51b-f5d501db9186",
            "build_id": "d6c8dfca-206e-47de-9883-a33bf6f6ca86",
            "round_number": 5,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-07-25T22:33:43.975855+00:00",
            "notes": "Get the [Soul Control](item_051aca60-1044-4184-bbbf-5aad8b12592a) power. This will allow you heal frequently during middle of combat. When you are low on health, use your ultimate and cancel it after about 1-2 seconds. You will keep 75% of your ult charge, but will be healed back to full HP. \n\nIt can also save you from a dangerous situation or bad position, for example if you are surrounded by multiple enemies. Lastly, this power lets you close the distance to the enemy without taking any damage. \n\nYou now fully transition into a melee playstyle and change your item loadout. Sell everything and at the very minimum, buy the following items:\n\n1.  [Gloomgauntlet](item_76cb8fe3-3c1f-4769-a1ec-a9c2dc510ba7) \n2. [Golden Monk](item_559b91a0-840b-4027-b99c-c5e6b609ae7c) \n3. [Weapon Jammer](item_72386db6-753e-413d-aa2a-f1389842f47f)\n4. [Keepsake of Chaos](item_5f5c7c4c-a559-43a0-9794-bdb866d2327e) \n\nIf you have extra cash, I highly recommend adding more survival items. Items that give damage reduction and armor ([Crusader Hydraulics](item_b64cee07-ca32-405d-987e-868b415bbc09)) are especially good. A cheap item that really helps your healing is [Siphon Gloves](item_099f8177-c2a4-4e13-b321-99349f8b1eb7).",
